{# FILES · CONFIGURE · SOURCE MODULES — what a module stores, and what it
   calls it.

   THE WORD IS THE MODULE'S, PRINTED VERBATIM. The core's file-source contract
   rules it: "the phrase is the module's… exactly as a configure section's
   label is", and the reason is that the word has to be the same one the
   module's own screens use. So this section states each declaration and
   offers no box to retype it; an organization that wants different words asks
   the module for them, in one place, rather than keeping a second vocabulary
   the module never sees.

   IT NEVER DECIDES WHO MAY SEE A FILE. The owning record does, always.

   THE SOURCES TAB READS WHO PUT WHAT HERE. This section reads the declaration
   itself — what the seam carries, and what a module has to say before its
   files can be listed at all. #}
{% extends '@UhifadhiStorage/base.html.twig' %}

{% block title %}Files &mdash; Source modules{% endblock %}

{% block shell_breadcrumbs %}<a href="{{ path(constant('Uhifadhi\\Storage\\Controller\\FilesSectionController::OVERVIEW')) }}">uhifadhi</a> / files / configure / source modules{% endblock %}

{% block shell_page_title %}Files{% endblock %}
{% block shell_page_subtitle %}Which module may put a file here, and what the hub calls it.{% endblock %}

{% block storage_page %}
    <div class="sxlead">
        <span class="t">{{ ux_icon('shell:file-text') }}<span><b>What a module stores, and what it calls it.</b> The declaration arrives with the package and leaves with it &middot; who may see a file is the record&rsquo;s answer.</span></span>
    </div>

    <div class="c" style="margin-bottom:20px">
        <span class="tab">Declared sources<span class="src">&middot; {{ rows|length }} installed &middot; {{ rows|filter(r => r.state == 'live')|length }} store</span></span>
        <table class="tbl">
            <thead><tr><th>Module</th><th>Registered as</th><th>Word for one file</th><th class="num">Files</th><th>Listed in the hub</th><th></th></tr></thead>
            <tbody>
            {% for row in rows %}
                <tr>
                    <td><b>{{ row.label }}</b></td>
                    <td><span class="mono d" style="font-size:11px">{{ row.slug }}</span></td>
                    <td>{% if row.fileWord %}<span class="fog">{{ row.fileWord }}</span>{% else %}<span class="mono d">&mdash;</span>{% endif %}</td>
                    <td class="num">{{ row.state == 'live' ? row.files|number_format : '&mdash;'|raw }}</td>
                    <td><span class="chip{{ row.state == 'live' ? ' ok' }}">{{ row.state == 'live' ? 'listed' : row.state }}</span></td>
                    <td><span class="mono d" style="font-size:11px">{{ row.state == 'live' ? row.records|number_format ~ ' records hold one' : 'declares no file store' }}</span></td>
                </tr>
            {% else %}
                <tr><td colspan="6"><span class="mono d">No module is installed that could declare a file store.</span></td></tr>
            {% endfor %}
            </tbody>
        </table>
        <div class="sxfoot"><span>Removing a module removes its source &middot; its bytes stay where they are</span></div>
    </div>

    <div class="c" style="margin-bottom:20px">
        <span class="tab">What the seam carries<span class="src">&middot; what a module has to declare</span></span>
        <table class="tbl">
            <thead><tr><th>Declaration</th><th>Exists</th><th>What it is for</th></tr></thead>
            <tbody>
            {% for line in seam %}
                <tr>
                    <td><span class="mono">{{ line.declaration }}</span></td>
                    <td><span class="mono {{ line.exists ? 'g' : 'w' }}">{{ line.exists ? 'yes' : 'no' }}</span></td>
                    <td>{{ line.purpose }}</td>
                </tr>
            {% endfor %}
            </tbody>
        </table>
        <div class="sxfoot"><span>{{ seam|filter(l => l.exists)|length }} of the {{ seam|length }} exist &middot; without them the hub must know each module by name</span></div>
    </div>

    <div class="c" style="margin-bottom:20px">
        <span class="tab">Imports<span class="src">&middot; none &middot; no import path exists</span></span>
        {# DRAWN WITH NO FIGURE BECAUSE THERE IS NOTHING TO COUNT. It is the one
           place a future import would show. #}
        <table class="tbl">
            <thead><tr><th>Path</th><th>State</th><th>What it would do</th></tr></thead>
            <tbody>
            <tr>
                <td><span class="mono d">bulk upload</span></td>
                <td><span class="chip">never</span></td>
                <td>a file arrives by being attached to a record, on that record&rsquo;s page</td>
            </tr>
            <tr>
                <td><span class="mono d">migrate from another store</span></td>
                <td><span class="chip warn">not built</span></td>
                <td>the one import that would be legitimate, and the row it would appear in</td>
            </tr>
            </tbody>
        </table>
        <div class="sxfoot"><span>No figure &mdash; nothing to count &middot; the one place a future import would show</span></div>
    </div>
{% endblock %}
